             <string>1 -&gt; 0.5, 1, 1.5, 2, 2.5, 3, 3.5, 4
2 -&gt; 4.5, 5, 5.5, 6, 6.5, 7, 7.5, 8, 8.5, 9, 9.5, 10
4 -&gt; 11, 12, 15, 20</string>
            </property>
           </widget>
          </item>
          <item>
           <widget class="QLabel" name="lblBandsHint">
            <property name="text">
             <string>Every line is built and solved for every condition. Short waves need panels that long waves do not, and solver cost is quadratic in the panel count — so a fine mesh carries the short end of the grid and a coarse one the long end. &quot;:&quot; works as well as &quot;→&quot;, ranges may be written 4..20..0.5, and anything after &quot;#&quot; is a note.</string>
            </property>
            <property name="wordWrap">
             <bool>true</bool>
            </property>
           </widget>
          </item>
